        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: speed up conf-sanity test_73e",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: speed up conf-sanity test_73e\n\ntest_73e adds 41 LNet networks on each remote server node, one\ndo_rpc_nodes call per network. Every call re-sources the test\nframework on the remote node, so each add took about 2 to 3\nseconds and the nodes were handled one after another.\n\nRun the 41 adds from a single do_node loop per node, and run the\nnodes in parallel. All 41 networks are still added on every node.\n\nOn a VM with one MDS and one OSS the test takes 99s, 91s, 92s\nand 90s (one run took 259s from slow cleanup unrelated to the\nloop), against 183s, 174s and 171s before. CI has more remote\nnodes and runs the test about 4117 times per 30 days at a mean\nof 715s, so the saving there is larger.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=conf-sanity env=ONLY=73e\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I0832caf07c4fe541c372187ac9b2cfbd5778c7cb\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70193\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nReviewed-by: Alex Deiter <adeiter@ddn.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
